The original Apache License 2.0 is retained in LICENSE, along with every source
copyright and license header. Original credits include kuloud and lbs.amap.com.
Civu platform patches are retained; see CIVU_PATCH.md. Birdtie changes native
debugMode to false in all build modes to suppress Android key/coordinate
argument logging. Birdtie also cancels controller event subscriptions, releases
the old widget reference and channel handler on disposal, and retires late
widget initialization without reopening callbacks. Birdtie compiles the Android
plugin against SDK 36 to match the app and the lifecycle dependency's AAR
metadata requirement; minimum SDK 21 and the AMap SDK version are retained.
The lifecycle regression test is new Birdtie code. No Civu product navigation,
business models, account state, keys, build output or example application is copied.

